capital rates, illiquidity premium, lapse or expense assumptions), with criteria for positioning within the range; 

- **iii. Materiality** — quantitative and qualitative materiality thresholds for adjustments, simplifications, disclosures and changes in approach; 

- **iv. Discounting** — construction of the risk-free yield curve, reference instruments, extrapolation beyond the last liquid point, ultimate forward rate (if any), currency and the top-down versus bottom-up approach; 

- **v. Flooring** — whether and at what level (contract, group, portfolio or entity) negative best-estimate liabilities or negative CSM should be floored, and the treatment of surrender value floors, UPR etc; 

- **vi. Risk margin** — scope of alignment between RBC’s risk margin with IndAS’s Risk Adjustment; 

- **vii. Illiquidity premium** — necessity and appropriateness of illiquidity premium; and 

**viii.** any other area where alternative approaches are possible. 

   - c. To prepare **draft template for submission of RBC data** by insurers to the Authority, covering the RBC Balance Sheet, the Ind AS-to-RBC reconciliation, Available and Required Capital by module, sensitivities, assumptions, and qualitative information. 

   - d. To make **recommendations on adopting** the converged framework for actuarial valuation of assets and liabilities under Section 13 and 49 of Insurance Act, 1938.
